## A Missed Generalization

```elixir
defmodule MissedGeneralization do
  # Copy your `randLetter` and `randString3` in this module

  def repRandom(_gens) do
    
  end
end
```

```elixir
ExUnit.start(autorun: false)

defmodule MissedGeneralizationTest do
  use ExUnit.Case, async: true

  test "it works" do
    seed = MCPrelude.mkSeed(1)
    gens = List.duplicate(MissedGeneralization.randLetter(), 3)
    {cs, _seed} = MissedGeneralization.repRandom(gens).(seed)
    assert to_string(cs) == MissedGeneralization.randString3()
  end
end

ExUnit.run()
```

## Formalizing the Pattern

https://mightybyte.github.io/monad-challenges/pages/ex4-3.html

```elixir
defprotocol Monad do
  # Protocols need at least one arguments for each function.
  # Replace `_?` with whatever you need.
  
  def bind(_?)

  # You can look for the `Collectable` protocol if you're feeling stuck.
  def return(_?)
end
```

